# Restricted singlet O2 with cylindrical symmetry: the two pi* electrons
# are spread over m=+1 and m=-1, half an electron in each spin orbital,
# instead of pairing in one complex orbital (-150.29075). The fractional
# occupations raise the energy by 55 mEh through the exact exchange; a
# pure functional gives both the same energy.
System O2.xyz
Basis cc-pVDZ
Method hyb_gga_xc_b3lyp
Multiplicity 1
Restricted true
ComplexBasis true
CylindricalSymmetry true
JKMethod Cholesky
DFTGrid 75 -302
ConvThr 1e-7
SaveChk complex_orbs_o2_b3lyp_cyl.chk
